    %main.sub-main
      .sub-content
        %p.tutorial-number Tutorial 01
        %h1 Flashing PteronautOS
        %p.sub-lead Build and install the hermetic firmware on the supported ESP8285 receiver target.

        %p Before connecting power, remove propulsive loads from the wing mechanism and make sure no servo can drive into a hard stop. Flashing is electrical work; the airframe should remain mechanically safe throughout the procedure.

        .video-embed
          %iframe{src: "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/h_MSh6qvfEAin", title: "Flashing PteronautOS tutorial", loading: "lazy", allow: "accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share", allowfullscreen: true}

        %h2 01 · Build the firmware
        %p Clone the repository, install PlatformIO, and build the dedicated receiver environment. The target enables the PteronautOS identity, ornithopter control, and the ESP8285/SX1280 hardware configuration.
        %pre
          %code pio run -e PteronautOS_ESP8285_2400_RX

        %h2 02 · Connect the receiver
        %p Wire a 3.3 V FTDI adapter to the UART pads and connect ground first. Do not apply 5 V to the ESP8285 logic pins. Disconnect the MPU6050 where the board revision shares its pins with the programming header.

        %h2 03 · Enter the bootloader
        %p Hold BOOT while powering the receiver. ESP8285 auto-reset is not reliable on every board, so keep BOOT asserted until the flashing tool has established communication.

        %h2 04 · Write the image
        %p Replace the serial device below with the port used by your adapter, then write the generated firmware image with DOUT flash mode.
        %pre
          %code esptool.py --port /dev/cu.usbserial-XXXX --baud 115200 --before no_reset write_flash --flash_mode dout --flash_size 1MB --flash_freq 40m 0x0 firmware.bin

        %h2 05 · Verify the installation
        %p Power-cycle the receiver without holding BOOT. Confirm that its WiFi access point and WebUI become available (SSID: <code>Pteronaut OS</code>, password: <code>flynatural</code>), then load the configuration and verify the target name before reconnecting servos.
        %p 
          Continue with the
          %a{href: "../../hardware/"} Hardware page 
          for pin maps and revision-specific wiring notes.
